        },
        "subject": "LU-20362 tests: replace \"ls -l\" with \"readlink\" in test_17i",
        "message": "LU-20362 tests: replace \"ls -l\" with \"readlink\" in test_17i\n\nIn sanity.sh test_17i, the fail_loc OBD_FAIL_MDS_READLINK_EPROTO\n(0x80000143) is set to simulate a readlink protocol error.\n\nHowever, on newer distributions (e.g., Ubuntu 26.04),\n`ls -l` invokes `listxattr()` to retrieve security contexts\nbefore calling `readlink()`.\nSince the fail_loc is flagged with OBD_FAIL_ONCE (0x80000000),\nthe `listxattr()` call consumes the fault injection,\nleaving the real `readlink()` unaffected.\nConsequently, `ls -l` succeeds and the test incorrectly passes.\n\nFix this by replacing `ls -l` with the dedicated `readlink` command.\nThis ensures the fail_loc is consumed precisely\nby the intended system call.\nThe `readlink` command is POSIX-compliant and available on all\nsupported distributions, so compatibility is preserved.\n\nTest-Parameters: fstype=ldiskfs mdtcount=4 mdscount=2 \t\t\tclientdistro=ubuntu2604 testlist=sanity\nSigned-off-by: Xiyang Wang <xiwang@ddn.com>\nChange-Id: I58248480ef6ae98dd8a0a1c9244192ba3f0a6a44\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
